{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546775-i-can-t-do-it","id":1546775,"title":"I can't do it:","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-08T18:01:27-08:00","id":1546775,"title":"I can't do it:","content":"The Grognard in me, says, that, mortals can soak lethal; I'm too set in my ways; however, perhaps the difficulty should be an eight (8)? Just that, if mortals have all that stamina, it's gotta be good for something other than surviving baseball-bat attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-08T18:25:06-08:00","id":1546777,"title":"","content":"Are you approaching rules as physics, or rules to set the tone of a story? Because in the latter case, there's some wide variation across the games. In Vampire, violence tends to be more grounded, but in Werewolf, even some monsters are treated as if they're made of Plasticine (vampires with minimal soak powers or Garou and Fera versus silver and/or gold, for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-08T18:51:19-08:00","id":1546781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546775-i-can-t-do-it?p=1546777#post1546777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you approaching rules as physics, or rules to set the tone of a story? Because in the latter case, there's some wide variation across the games. In Vampire, violence tends to be more grounded, but in Werewolf, even some monsters are treated as if they're made of Plasticine (vampires with minimal soak powers or Garou and Fera versus silver and/or gold, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>Having played V:tM since the early '90's, soaking lethal is engrained in my thinking and I feel like, playing later editions, that not letting PCs' soak lethal, kind of cheats their characters out of their stamina-stat. <br /> <br /> We also use OWoD as a sort of fantasy-game, in which, the players were mortal, and magical-swords always did aggravated; mortal-players not being able to soak lethal, makes the magical-weapons kinda-moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-08T20:12:04-08:00","id":1546786,"title":"","content":"Whether or not characters can soak lethal doesn't seem to be some sort of grognard thing. Mages were never able to soak like that without using magic, Armor has always existed. Magical weapons in most games are a lot more important than doing damage that tougher supernaturals can soak (though flaming swords and silver bullets have their place too).<br /> <br /> A magical sword that can strike incorporeal entities like characters using astral projection powers is a lot bigger deal than unsoakable damage. Stamina/Soak are pretty weak in the oWoD ruleset. A magical sword that does +2HL of damage is almost the same as one that does damage a mortal-scale character can't soak (Stamina 5 soaks ~2ish damage on average, with a big of variation on edition/interpretation). I've had mortals take down vampires with mundane (if military grade) firearms and lots of bashing damage (yes, even with the halving of bashing damage vampires do).<br /> <br /> If you want to make Stamina useful... make it useful? There's more to life than fighting. Werewolf, Mage, and Changeling (by virtue of not dealing with the dead and undead who are less worried about physical endurance) tend to include a lot more examples of Stamina based actions. Werewolves with high Stamina can run huge distances in lupus by pushing their bodies to ignore food and rest. Mages need Stamina for their most potent rituals. Etc.<br /> <br /> Sure, you can make Stamina better in combat, but that has its own issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-08T21:23:36-08:00","id":1546789,"title":"","content":"Oh it is absolutely possible to put down vampires with firearms. Just takes a few extra bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T05:55:45-08:00","id":1546863,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I started playing back in the days when humans could soak lethal damage with Stamina and I still like that idea. It makes sense that tougher humans are more resistant to damage, even bullets or blades. Then those weapons can do more damage if they seem insufficiently dangerous - which they did back in early editions.<br /> <br /> Then again, I also want vampires to be able to soak aggravates damage with Stamina except for sunlight, fire, and faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T16:18:21-08:00","id":1546940,"title":"","content":"After some considerations, I'm thinking that, from a ST PoV, that mortals not soaking lethal makes the game go a bit faster, however, perhaps, important mortals like NPCs and PCs, can soak, but difficulty eight? Sounds about right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-13T20:10:32-08:00","id":1546952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546775-i-can-t-do-it?p=1546940#post1546940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After some considerations, I'm thinking that, from a ST PoV, that mortals not soaking lethal makes the game go a bit faster, however, perhaps, important mortals like NPCs and PCs, can soak, but difficulty eight? Sounds about right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds about plot armor.<br /> <br /> How about, instead of trusting your important NPCs into gun fights with Fairy Tales monsters, why not have them be smart, manipulative and resourceful, and being the kind of ones that stay on their highly secured penthouses?<br /> <br /> As for the PCs well, we as STs will always do our best to protect them, but sometimes stupidity just simply cannot be cured...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 12-13-2024, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-18T18:57:16-08:00","id":1547140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546775-i-can-t-do-it?p=1546952#post1546952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> . . . Fairy Tales monsters, . . ..</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't call the Low-Clans that. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}